IMPORT prelude

§ `Fact vocabulary (from bench/schema-l4.md, verbatim)`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER
      `confined in us hospital`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuous confinement days`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `claim made setting out basis`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- Supporting helpers (pre-defined -- call them, do not redefine them)

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `Coverage logic`

-- 1.1(2): the applicable premium for the policy period has been paid.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`premium paid` claim MEANS isJust (claim's `premium paid month`)

-- 1.3: written confirmation, from the medical provider, of a wellness visit
-- with a qualified medical provider -- the visit no later than the 6th
-- month anniversary, the confirmation no later than the 7th. 1.1(3)'s
-- "still pending" is treated as equivalent to "satisfied" here; see
-- NOTES.md for the reasoning.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit condition satisfied` claim MEANS
       claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`
   AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
   AND `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7

-- 1.2: cancellation for fraud.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fraud occurred` claim MEANS isJust (claim's `fraud month`)

-- 1.2: cancellation for misrepresentation or material withholding of
-- information.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`misrepresentation occurred` claim MEANS isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)

-- 1.2 / 4.6: the policy is automatically canceled at the end of the
-- one-year policy term.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy term has expired` claim MEANS
  claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN claim's `policy term months`

-- 1.1: the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at the time of hospitalization` claim MEANS
       claim's `agreement signed`
   AND `premium paid` claim
   AND `wellness visit condition satisfied` claim
   AND NOT `fraud occurred` claim
   AND NOT `misrepresentation occurred` claim
   AND NOT `policy term has expired` claim

-- 2.1: the hospitalization must be for sickness or accidental injury --
-- not, e.g., a deliberate act that is neither.
GIVEN ground IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ground is sickness or accidental injury` ground MEANS
  CONSIDER ground
    WHEN Sickness THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither THEN FALSE

-- 2.2: at least one day of continuous confinement, to trigger the daily
-- benefit. The 365-day cap in 2.2 limits how many days are payable; on its
-- own words it does not disqualify a longer stay altogether, so it is not
-- enforced here as a coverage gate -- see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`had continuous confinement` claim MEANS
  fromMaybe 0 (claim's `continuous confinement days`) GREATER THAN 0

-- 2.1 / 2.2 / 2.3: the benefit-trigger conditions -- sickness-or-injury
-- ground, confinement in a US hospital, some continuous confinement, and a
-- claim made setting out the basis for it.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`benefit conditions satisfied` claim MEANS
       `ground is sickness or accidental injury` (claim's `hospitalization ground`)
   AND claim's `confined in us hospital`
   AND `had continuous confinement` claim
   AND claim's `claim made setting out basis`

-- 3.1: the event causing the sickness or accidental injury must not arise,
-- directly or indirectly, out of any of the four listed activities, and
-- the claimant must be under 80 at the time of hospitalization.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`event excluded under the general exclusions` claim MEANS
       `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
   OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

-- 4.2.1: once a dispute has arisen, arbitration must be commenced within
-- three months of the day the parties became unable to settle. If they
-- have not yet reached that impasse, the three-month clock has not
-- started, so this is vacuously satisfied -- see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration commenced timely` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST u  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (u PLUS 3)

-- 4.2.1: where a dispute has arisen, timely arbitration and the issuance of
-- a valid award are conditions precedent to liability. Where no dispute has
-- arisen, this clause does not bite.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration precondition satisfied` claim MEANS
  IF claim's `dispute arisen`
  THEN `arbitration commenced timely` claim AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`
  ELSE TRUE

-- 4.2.1: in no case may recovery on the policy be sought before the
-- expiration of sixty days after written proof of claim has been
-- submitted. Sixty days is approximated as two months here, to match the
-- granularity of the given month fields -- see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery not sought prematurely` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r THEN
      CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST w THEN r AT LEAST (w PLUS 2)

-- 4.2: the arbitration and no-action preconditions to liability, taken
-- together.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration and no-action conditions satisfied` claim MEANS
       `arbitration precondition satisfied` claim
   AND `recovery not sought prematurely` claim

§ `Coverage decision`

-- True exactly when a benefit is payable on the claim.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered claim IF
       `policy in effect at the time of hospitalization` claim
   AND `benefit conditions satisfied` claim
   AND NOT `event excluded under the general exclusions` claim
   AND `arbitration and no-action conditions satisfied` claim
